  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">InfraCo Africa Development is a facility of the Private Infrastructure Development Group and has been designed to assume the risks and costs of early-stage project development in lower income countries in Africa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This activity InfraCo Africa Development is a facility of the Private Infrastructure Development Group and has been designed to assume the risks and costs of early-stage project development in lower income countries in Africa is a component of PIDG2 - Second phase of FCDO&apos;s Support to the Private Infrastructure Development Group .  reported by FCDO with a funding type of 109 - Multilateral organisation and a budget of &#xa3;47,920,500. This project benefits Africa, regional. It works in the following sector(s): Energy generation, non-renewable sources, unspecified, Information and communication technology (ICT), Transport policy and administrative management, Low-cost housing, Agricultural services, Sanitation - large systems.</narrative>
  </description>
